These have bounds checks (`cwords >= words`). So those are probably fine.

What about line 788?
```c
ucbits = FLAC__BITS_PER_WORD - br->consumed_bits;
b = br->buffer[cwords] << br->consumed_bits;
```

This is executed before the main while loop when `cwords < words` (line 782 check). So this should be fine.

Let me look at a different angle. Maybe the bug is in `FLAC__bitreader_read_unary_unsigned` at line 694:
